    <h1>GenLayer Intelligent Contracts and Decentralized AI Consensus</h1>

    <p>
      Traditional smart contracts work well when every rule can be evaluated
      deterministically from onchain values. Many real-world agreements,
      however, depend on meaning, context, and qualitative evidence.
    </p>

    <p>
      GenLayer Intelligent Contracts extend blockchain applications by allowing
      AI validators to evaluate public information. Multiple validators
      independently examine the same evidence and use decentralized consensus
      to agree on the result.
    </p>

    <p>
      This makes it possible to verify requirements that cannot be reduced to
      simple numerical comparisons. A sponsorship contract can define a public
      brief, receive evidence from a creator, and ask validators whether the
      submitted work meaningfully satisfies that brief.
    </p>

    <p>
      ProofSponsor applies this process to sponsored content. The sponsor
      publishes the requirements, the creator submits a public deliverable,
      and GenLayer validators determine whether the work meets the declared
      conditions.
    </p>

    <p>
      The wallet-specific proof marker below binds this public evidence page to
      the creator wallet used for the onchain submission.
    </p>

